+
+# ===========================================================================
+# Windows reparse points
+# ===========================================================================
+internal/buildcache	TestSweepDoesNotFollowAReparsedEntry	windows	windows	host-capability	cache sweep refuses to traverse a reparse point inside an entry
+internal/buildcache	TestSweepDoesNotFollowAReparsedCacheRoot	windows	windows	host-capability	cache sweep refuses to traverse a reparsed cache root
+internal/scopes	TestCollectStaysFailSafeOnRedirectedWindowsScopes	windows	windows	host-capability	GC stays fail-safe when a Windows scope is redirected by a reparse point
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# Windows `.cmd` launchers
+# ===========================================================================
+internal/runtimestore	TestWindowsPostInstallWrappersForwardArgumentsPathAndExitCode	windows	-	-	the installed `.cmd` wrapper forwards arguments, PATH and exit code through cmd.exe
+internal/runtimestore	TestInstallSingleCommandAndShims	linux,darwin,windows	-	-	writes the `run.cmd` Windows launcher and asserts its `@echo off` payload
+internal/runtimestore	TestRuntimeCommandPath	linux,darwin,windows	-	-	maps a `tool.cmd` Windows launcher back to its command name
+internal/runtimestore	TestCompiledShimsStageWithoutLaunchThenPostInstallForwardExactly	linux,darwin	windows	platform-control	compiled shims stage without launching, then forward exactly (POSIX post-install fixture)
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# Unix ownership and permission
+# ===========================================================================
+internal/buildcache	TestUnixProtectedStateMatrix	linux,darwin	-	-	unix ownership and mode matrix for protected cache state
+internal/buildcache	TestUnixProtectionHelperFailuresFailClosed	linux,darwin	-	-	unix protection helpers fail closed rather than degrading the boundary
+internal/config	TestBootstrapAndAddProject	linux,darwin,windows	-	-	asserts the manager config is written with private (0o600) ownership bits on unix
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# No-follow: link traversal is refused, never followed
+# ===========================================================================
+internal/buildcache	TestSweepDoesNotFollowSymlinkedEntries	linux,darwin	-	-	cache sweep refuses to traverse symlinked entries
+internal/buildcache	TestSweepDoesNotFollowASymlinkedCacheRoot	linux,darwin	-	-	cache sweep refuses to traverse a symlinked cache root
+internal/buildcache	TestRetireEntryRemovesLinksWithoutFollowingThem	linux,darwin	-	-	entry retirement removes links without following them
+internal/buildcache	TestUnixRejectsEntrySymlinkAndUnprotectedCacheRoot	linux,darwin	-	-	rejects a symlinked entry and an unprotected cache root
+internal/scopes	TestCollectStaysFailSafeOnRedirectedUnixScopes	linux,darwin	-	-	GC stays fail-safe when a unix scope is redirected by a link
+internal/buildsource	TestRejectsSpecialFile	linux,darwin	-	-	build source enumeration rejects a non-regular file
+internal/gitops	TestArchiveRejectsLinks	linux,darwin	windows	host-capability	archiving refuses a tree containing links (needs `ln`, absent from the Windows job PATH)
