+# Protocol platform exclusion -- asserted, never merely omitted.
+#
+# The rc.5 qualification vector marks linux `excluded` (until_task
+# TASK-260728-1skseh), so `internal/godriver` does not execute there.  This
+# case proves the exclusion is real fail-closed behaviour: an uncovered
+# platform is refused BEFORE the worker starts.  It is required on every
+# runner, including the one where the package is otherwise excluded.
+# ===========================================================================
+internal/godriver	TestProbeRejectsAnUncoveredPlatformBeforeTheWorker	linux,darwin,windows	-	-	an uncovered inventory platform (including linux) is rejected before the worker starts
+
+# ===========================================================================
